<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 74.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics on a no-flux corneal patch whose continuous k_c is pinned to 2.397e-05 m at 508 Ma, and places that field beside the Tyrrell cast TMP 2023.003.0003. The sweep, ablation, specimen segmentation, and dispersion goodness-of-fit are not yet accepted as closing evidence. Overall 74.4/100 (faithfulness 69.7, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 63ace896bba72dd95b1823861b5b9936be9cf066; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 60, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 63ace896bba72dd95b1823861b5b9936be9cf066, image/png, 661168 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 8c788c0b684071e171d8a48b94401bc5386b600a5228f9624b970e75fdc1be4f (sha256 8c788c0b684071e171d8a48b94401bc5386b600a5228f9624b970e75fdc1be4f), spec_fingerprint 6e60ae9de13486d021af674ae24c3fe415cc4c359fddd14174f41704efc81a34. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6e60ae9de13486d021af674ae24c3fe415cc4c359fddd14174f41704efc81a34; artifact_sha256: 8c788c0b684071e171d8a48b94401bc5386b600a5228f9624b970e75fdc1be4f. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reacting-diffusing state can be unstable at a finite wavenumber. | Paterson et al. 2011: Emu Bay eyes 2-3 cm, at least 16000 hexagonal lenses, about 515 Ma. | Daley and Edgecombe 2014: Burgess Shale A. canadensis has paired stalked eyes and a triradial oral cone. | Van Roy and Briggs 2011: Fezouata anomalocaridids (488-472 Ma) are larger than Cambrian bodies.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b) = (0.10, 0.90), Dv/Du = 20, Du set so lambda_c = 8 cells = 2.397e-05 m. | Hexagonal spacing on a 2.5 cm hemisphere with 16000 lenses, about 266 µm. That reconstruction is not a published lens diameter.; transfer_boundary: Burgess Shale compressions do not resolve a 24 µm pigment lattice. The cast photograph is organism-scale. | Lubensky et al. 2011 is cited as a non-transfer: the Drosophila R8 lattice is not a Turing instability.; does_not_claim: That a, b, Du, Dv were measured in anomalocaridid cornea. | That the Commons length of about 20 cm is a Daley and Edgecombe morphometric. | That Fezouata giants kept this same k_c. Only that a tissue-local wavenumber does not have to grow with body length.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Accept a Du diffusivity sweep and show that lambda_c increases monotonically across the stated range.",
        "remediation needed: R2: Accept the equal-diffusion negative control and the linear-reaction ablation, with a pattern-std ratio against the Turing run.",
        "remediation needed: R3: Segment the real Tyrrell cast (foreground fraction, circularity, structure-tensor coherency) and keep those values distinct from their references.",
        "remediation needed: R4: Report goodness-of-fit of the stencil growth rate against the numerical growth rate (Pearson r, RMSE, KS) and require Pearson r > 0.98." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.44e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

