<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) (Anomalocaris canadensis)",
        "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) faithfully reproduces Anomalocaris canadensis morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Anomalocaris canadensis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Anomalocaris canadensis" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Fezouata giants kept this same k_c. Only that a tissue-local wavenumber does not have to grow with body length.",
        "does_not_claim: That a, b, Du, Dv were measured in anomalocaridid cornea.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Commons length of about 20 cm is a Daley and Edgecombe morphometric.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Hexagonal spacing on a 2.5 cm hemisphere with 16000 lenses, about 266 µm. That reconstruction is not a published lens diameter.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b) = (0.10, 0.90), Dv/Du = 20, Du set so lambda_c = 8 cells = 2.397e-05 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Daley and Edgecombe 2014: Burgess Shale A. canadensis has paired stalked eyes and a triradial oral cone.",
        "reported_in_source: Paterson et al. 2011: Emu Bay eyes 2-3 cm, at least 16000 hexagonal lenses, about 515 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reacting-diffusing state can be unstable at a finite wavenumber.",
        "reported_in_source: Van Roy and Briggs 2011: Fezouata anomalocaridids (488-472 Ma) are larger than Cambrian bodies.",
        "transfer_boundary: Burgess Shale compressions do not resolve a 24 µm pigment lattice. The cast photograph is organism-scale.",
        "transfer_boundary: Lubensky et al. 2011 is cited as a non-transfer: the Drosophila R8 lattice is not a Turing instability." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Anomalocaris canadensis (Middle Cambrian (Burgess Shale, 508 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Anomalocaris" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Anomalocaris canadensis; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reacting-diffusing state can be unstable at a finite wavenumber. | Paterson et al. 2011: Emu Bay eyes 2-3 cm, at least 16000 hexagonal lenses, about 515 Ma. | Daley and Edgecombe 2014: Burgess Shale A. canadensis has paired stalked eyes and a triradial oral cone. | Van Roy and Briggs 2011: Fezouata anomalocaridids (488-472 Ma) are larger than Cambrian bodies.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b) = (0.10, 0.90), Dv/Du = 20, Du set so lambda_c = 8 cells = 2.397e-05 m. | Hexagonal spacing on a 2.5 cm hemisphere with 16000 lenses, about 266 µm. That reconstruction is not a published lens diameter.; transfer_boundary: Burgess Shale compressions do not resolve a 24 µm pigment lattice. The cast photograph is organism-scale. | Lubensky et al. 2011 is cited as a non-transfer: the Drosophila R8 lattice is not a Turing instability.; does_not_claim: That a, b, Du, Dv were measured in anomalocaridid cornea. | That the Commons length of about 20 cm is a Daley and Edgecombe morphometric. | That Fezouata giants kept this same k_c. Only that a tissue-local wavenumber does not have to grow with body length.]; phenomenon_size: 24 µm (2.352e-05 m, log10=-4.629 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 24 µm to 5.3 cm): 24 µm:anomalocaris-canadensis-bioelectric-polarity, 74 µm:anomalocaris-canadensis-vertex-packing, 1.2 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength, 2.4 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-clock-wavefront, 5.3 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-morphogen-condensation, 6.5 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-elastic-buckling, 7.3 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-flux-canalization, 1.0 cm:anomalocaris-canadensis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09920>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10689>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015302108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1666/13-067> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Anomalocaris>,
        <https://www.morphosource.org/Search/index?search=Anomalocaris> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Trilobite Segmentation & Eye Fossil Series" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 5.08e+02 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Middle Cambrian (Burgess Shale, 508 Ma)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
